PG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/SEUtahStrat.JPG/500px-SEUtahStrat.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Jurassic through Permian stratigraphy of the Colorado Plateau area of southeastern Utah that makes up much of the famous prominent rock formations in protected areas such as Capitol Reef National Park and Canyonlands National Park.  From top to bottom, (Jurassic to Permian): (6)-Rounded tan domes of the Navajo Sandstone, (5)-(dark)-layered red Kayenta Formation, (4)-cliff-forming, vertically jointed, red Wingate Sandstone, (3)-slope-forming, purplish Chinle Formation, (2)-layered, lighter-red Moenkopi Formation, and (1)-white, layered Cutler Formation sandstone.  Picture from Glen Canyon National Recreation Area, Utah.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASEUtahStrat.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Eocyclotosaurus_wellesi1DB.jpg/500px-Eocyclotosaurus_wellesi1DB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Eocyclotosaurus_wellesi1DB.jpg/1280px-Eocyclotosaurus_wellesi1DB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Eocyclotosaurus_wellesi1DB.jpg/500px-Eocyclotosaurus_wellesi1DB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Eocyclotosaurus","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEocyclotosaurus_wellesi1DB.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg/500px-EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg/1280px-EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg/500px-EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Soil measuring and surveying device","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Estructura-suelo.jpg/500px-Estructura-suelo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Estructura-suelo.jpg/500px-Estructura-suelo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A, B, and C represent the soil profile, a notation firstly coined by Vasily Dokuchaev (1846–1903), the father of pedology. Here, A is the topsoil; B is a regolith; C is a saprolite (a less-weathered regolith); the bottom-most layer represents the bedrock.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEstructura-suelo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Soil_erosion%2C_Southfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_367917.jpg/500px-Soil_erosion%2C_Southfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_367917.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Soil_erosion%2C_Southfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_367917.jpg/500px-Soil_erosion%2C_Southfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_367917.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Desertification","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASoil_erosion%2C_Southfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_367917.jpg"}],"sounds":{"soil":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d9/En-us-soil.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.or